abstract = {The "bouncing" behavior of astronauts when moving outside the lunar module can easily cause impact damage to the astronauts' bones, and a spacesuit intelligent assistive device is designed according to the requirements of the new spacesuit to buffer the impact caused by the "bouncing" behavior of astronauts. In order to realize that the spacesuit intelligent assistive device cooperates with the astronaut's gait, a hybrid CNN-LSTM spacesuit intelligent assistive device gait prediction model is constructed in this study by using CNN (Convolutional Neural Network) and LSTM (Long Short-Term Memory) models of deep learning. First, a hybrid state model of the kinematics and dynamics of the assistive device was established, and the lower limb motion data and plantar pressure data of the human body during walking were collected using an IMU (Inertial Measurement Unit) and a pressure sensor in a simulated lunar low-gravity environment, and data preprocessing was performed using data normalization and Kalman filtering methods. Second, a hybrid CNN-LSTM gait prediction model was constructed, and the hyperparameters of the LSTM model were optimized using GA (Genetic Algorithm), and the gait prediction model was used to predict the angular velocities of the right lower limb segments and the corresponding plantar pressures when the human body walked. Finally, the model evaluation and case calculation results verified that the hybrid CNN-LSTM gait prediction model has a high prediction accuracy, compared to the Transformer model, the hybrid CNN-LSTM model demonstrated with an 8 % reduction in RMSE (Root Mean Square Error) and 17 % reduction in MAE (Mean Absolute Error) for hip joint angular velocity predictions, while achieving 11 % lower RMSE and 12 % lower MAE for plantar pressure predictions, and that the model prediction results can be used to determine the working state of the drive joints of the assistive device and the amount of force applied. It provides a new method for human gait prediction, and at the same time lays the foundation for the cooperative control of the drive buffers of the spacesuit intelligent assistive device.}
}

